# Applies to every build whose context is the repo root: web/Dockerfile (via
# docker-compose and the CI frontend job) and fly/Dockerfile (via `flyctl deploy`).
# BuildKit reads .dockerignore from the *context root*, so web/.dockerignore stopped
# applying the moment web's context moved up here — without this file `COPY web/ ./web/`
# would drop a stale host node_modules on top of the one `npm ci` just built, and the
# image would build green against the wrong dependency tree.
#
# Do NOT exclude backend/, web/, packages/ or fly/ — all four are copied by fly/Dockerfile.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Test/build output
web/coverage
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/.vite
mobile/.expo
mobile/android
mobile/ios

# Local runtime state — the DB is a Fly volume in production
data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Docs and design assets: nothing in any image reads these
docs
design
releases
**/*.md
!README.md
